The function checks every pair of elements and keeps the pair whose product is largest. It returns the two numbers in the order they appear in the array, which matches the test output `(7, 8)`. Because all pairs are compared, it also handles negative numbers correctly, where two large negatives can give the highest product. It runs in O(n²) time.

```python
def max_Product(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    if n < 2:
        return None
    x, y = arr[0], arr[1]
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i + 1, n):
            if arr[i] * arr[j] > x * y:
                x, y = arr[i], arr[j]
    return (x, y)
```

